    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance so responders can identify the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with vertical reflective posts on both sides to guide responders during low-visibility or nighttime response.\n• Keep the full length of the driveway clear of parked vehicles and equipment so responders can reach the residence without stopping to reposition.\n• Maintain driveway width and overhead clearance along the entire drive to allow fire apparatus and ambulances to pass without obstruction.\n• Identify and mark a turnaround point near the residence so apparatus can reposition without backing the full length of the driveway.\n• Clear a staging area near the residence that responders can use to park and work without blocking the driveway.\n• Keep gates along the driveway unlocked or equipped with a Knox-Box or standard breakaway lock so responders are not delayed at entry.\n• Trim landscaping along the driveway that narrows the travel path or reduces driver sightlines.\n• Mark any secondary foot path or route around the rear of the residence so responders can orient quickly on arrival.\n• Post a site map or address placard near the driveway entrance showing the residence location and any secondary access routes across the open terrain."
